 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to industrial\nhemp development",
    "basePrintNo": "S8496",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8496-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §519, Ag & Mkts L",
    "lawSection": "Agriculture and Markets Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8496\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to indus-\ntrial hemp development\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to encourage the use of industrial\nhemp grown in New York by businesses.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISION:\n\nThe bill would amend section 519 of the Agriculture and Markets Law to\nupdate the hemp economic development section of law to clarify that the\nCommissioner shall work with the urban development corporation, the New\nYork State hemp workgroup created in Cannabis Law, and representatives\nof industries that currently use, or may potentially use, industrial\nhemp in their products, to develop and promote the use of hemp by busi-\nnesses for purposes such as packaging, construction, and other uses,\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew York is a leader in the cultivation and processing of hemp, espe-\ncially for cannabinoid hemp. The market for New York industrial hemp is\nstill developing and the state needs to take an active role in research-\ning, identifying, and promoting hemp to industries that may incorporate\nit into their products. For example, as the market for sustainable,\nbiodegradable, non-petroleum-based packaging grows, so do the opportu-\nnities for New York produced industrial hemp as an ingredient in these\nproducts. This legislation will encourage renewed focus by the State to\nwork with growers, processors and businesses that are end users to\nexpand market opportunities.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nUndetermined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
